Third-party data files
======================

None. This repository contains no market data files from any venue.

Every venue-format frame in the tree is synthetic: invented prices, sizes, ids
and timestamps, written in each venue's wire format by
scripts/make-synthetic-fixtures.py from a fixed seed, named synthetic-*, and
listed with its sha256 in tests/fixtures/SHA256SUMS, which the same script
writes:

  services/capture-rust/tests/fixtures/synthetic-*    replay test sessions (their golden
                                                      hashes, synthetic-*.sha256, are pinned
                                                      from the replay output, not generated)
  tests/fixtures/bronze/synthetic-*                   one frame per bronze table
  docs/research/2026-08-26-v3-spikes/*/synthetic-*    the S2 and S5 spike samples

The manifest proves a file is what the committed generator writes, not that
the generator invents its values, so a review must read the generator's diff.

Hand-written synthetic rows, invented values on round numbers, for the
ClickHouse schema test (scripts/clickhouse-schema-test.sh):

  tests/clickhouse/bars.jsonl
  tests/clickhouse/book.jsonl
  tests/clickhouse/trades_block1.jsonl
  tests/clickhouse/trades_block2.jsonl

The platform's own measurements, no venue data: recovery times written by
`make chaos` (scripts/chaos/):

  scripts/chaos/results/2026-08-26.tsv
  scripts/chaos/results/2026-08-27.tsv

Gate (i) of scripts/check-docs.sh (scripts/check_docs.py) fails CI on a data
file, found by extension or by content (JSON lines, CSV, TSV, Parquet, Avro,
pcap, a compressed stream) whatever its name or path, that is neither in
tests/fixtures/SHA256SUMS at its hash nor listed by exact path in this file
with its source and terms; on a synthetic-* file the manifest does not list;
and on a committed notebook with outputs (under legacy/, unless listed below).

Market data is fetched by a user's own running stack from each venue's public
endpoints, stays on that user's machine, and is subject to that provider's
terms (README, "What this is, and data terms"). `make record-fixtures` records
real frames into services/capture-rust/tests/recorded/, which is git-ignored.

Earlier commits in this repository's history contain recorded venue frames that
have since been replaced by the synthetic files above. History is not rewritten
(docs/adr/ADR-029-research-production-parity-contract.md, Outcome 2026-11).

Venue values in immutable documents
===================================

Dated snapshots and Accepted ADRs are never rewritten (CLAUDE.md, Immutability),
so a venue price, volume or market-data count that was true when one was
written stays in it. These files carry such values, as found by a sweep on
2026-11-26. They are measurements of a run on the maintainer's machine or
single illustrative samples, kept for the record, not a data set and not
offered as one. The values themselves are deliberately not repeated here.

Every other document is editable and carries none: it states a ratio, a size
in bytes, a duration, or a pointer to the platform table or dated snapshot that
holds the figure. Gate (j) of scripts/check-docs.sh fails CI on a count of
captured data in any tracked Markdown file outside the immutable directories;
the rule, the directories it exempts and the opt-out for the platform's own
figures are stated once, in scripts/check_docs.py, gate (j).

