Generated test expectations
===========================

platform/k2gen/tests/golden/ holds what the compiler emits from the synthetic
fixture set, for its tests to compare against; nothing in it is source data.
Gate (i) reads its text files as such only while its README.md opens with the
marker line scripts/check_docs.py names (GOLDEN_MARK). A product's seed,
contracts/<domain>/<product>/seeds/<name>.csv, passes gate (i) only when its
product file declares it synthetic; real reference data is listed here instead.

Third-party reference values in code
====================================

The Kraken book checksum tests (services/capture-rust/src/exchanges/kraken.rs,
services/capture-rust/src/decimal.rs, tests/test_lake_book.py and the S1 spike
under docs/research/2026-08-26-v3-spikes/s1-kraken-checksum/) use the worked
example published in Kraken's WebSocket v2 book documentation,
https://docs.kraken.com/api/docs/guides/spot-ws-book-v2, as a test vector for
the checksum algorithm. It is quoted for interoperability testing, not as data.

